<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A short, non-interactive hint for a control, shown on hover or keyboard focus.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/tooltip)

<%= embed AppicaUI::TooltipPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
TooltipProvider do # once, high in the layout
  Tooltip do
    TooltipTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger, variant: :outline, icon: true, aria_label: "Add to favorites") { Icon(:heart) } }
    TooltipContent { "Add to favorites" }
  end
end
```

The bubble opens after the delay on hover and at once on keyboard focus, and closes on leave, blur, Escape or a click
on the trigger. A `TooltipProvider` shares the `delay:` and lets a neighbour open instantly while one is open or just
closed. The trigger is described by the bubble (`aria-describedby`) - it is not its name, so icon-only triggers still
need an `aria_label:`. For content everyone must reach use a [Popover](<%= page_path(:popover) %>).

